<h1>Culture Media x AEF<br>3% Membership Growth Campaign</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Marketing &amp; Creative Services RFP Response &nbsp;|&nbsp; February 2026</p>

<hr>

<!-- ============================================ -->
<!-- ABOUT THE CLIENT                             -->
<!-- ============================================ -->

<h2>About the Client &mdash; The Alberta Equestrian Federation</h2>

<p>The Alberta Equestrian Federation is the province's sole governing body for equestrian sport and industry, recognized by the Government of Alberta since 1978. AEF serves nearly 15,000 members across more than 425 Alberta communities, covering everything from competitive sport to recreational trail riding. Their programs include coaching certification, Learn to Ride/Drive, Wild Rose competitions, trail initiatives, and equine welfare advocacy.</p>

<p>Every membership includes $5M liability insurance and $40K AD&amp;D coverage, making it one of the highest-value equestrian memberships in the country.</p>

<div class="stats-box">
  <h3 style="margin-top:0; border:none; padding:0;">AEF at a Glance</h3>
  <table style="border:none; margin:6pt 0 0 0;">
    <tr>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 20pt 2pt 0; width:50%;">&bull;&nbsp; 15,000 members across Alberta</td>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 0;">&bull;&nbsp; Serving Alberta's equine community since 1978</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 20pt 2pt 0;">&bull;&nbsp; 425+ communities represented</td>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 0;">&bull;&nbsp; Coaching, competition, recreation, trail riding, welfare</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 20pt 2pt 0;">&bull;&nbsp; 22,000+ newsletter subscribers</td>
      <td style="border:none; padding:2pt 0;">&bull;&nbsp; $5M liability + $40K AD&amp;D with every membership</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<p>The goal: grow total AEF membership by 3% over the next four months through a targeted digital marketing campaign. That means reaching the thousands of equestrian participants across Alberta who ride, train, and compete but haven't signed up yet.</p>

<!-- PAGE BREAK -->
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-special-character:line-break;">

