<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-special-character:line-break;">

<!-- ============================================ -->
<!-- BARRIERS TO GROWTH                           -->
<!-- ============================================ -->

<h2>The Barriers to Membership Growth</h2>

<p>AEF doesn't have a competition problem. It has an awareness and clarity problem. We'll fix that.</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Barrier</th>
    <th>What's Happening</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Limited Awareness</td>
    <td>Many equestrian participants across Alberta don't know AEF exists or what it does for them.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Unclear Benefits</td>
    <td>$5M liability insurance, $40K AD&amp;D coverage, and funding programs aren't reaching the right people.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>&ldquo;Not For Me&rdquo; Perception</td>
    <td>Recreational riders, trail riders, and hobbyists think AEF is only for competitive equestrians.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Transactional Engagement</td>
    <td>Members renew for insurance but don't feel connected to a community or movement.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="callout">
  <p style="margin-bottom:0;">Our approach: reframe AEF membership from a transaction to a statement of identity. When you're part of the equestrian community in Alberta, AEF membership is what responsible participants do. Protection, value, and belonging.</p>
</div>

<!-- PAGE BREAK -->
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-special-character:line-break;">

<!-- ============================================ -->
<!-- STRATEGIC APPROACH                           -->
<!-- ============================================ -->

<h2>Strategic Approach &mdash; One Campaign, Four Audience Pathways</h2>

<h3>1. Barn Owners, Facilities &amp; Coaches (High Priority / Multiplier Audience)</h3>
<p>One facility requiring AEF membership can bring in dozens of riders.</p>
<ul>
  <li>AEF membership protects your facility, students, and reputation</li>
  <li>Professional liability framing, not fear-based</li>
  <li>Toolkit assets for facilities to share with riders and boarders</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Broader Equestrian Community (Recreational &amp; Non-Competitive)</h3>
<p>Trail riders and hobbyists who don't realize AEF is for everyone.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Normalize AEF membership as part of riding in Alberta</li>
  <li>Plain-language benefit breakdowns and community stories</li>
  <li>&ldquo;I ride in Alberta. I'm AEF.&rdquo; &mdash; identity-driven messaging</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Families, Youth &amp; New Riders (Growth Segment)</h3>
<p>Parents need reassurance. New riders need structure. AEF provides both.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Safety-first messaging: insurance as peace of mind</li>
  <li>Highlight Learn to Ride/Drive and coaching pathways</li>
  <li>Welcoming tone that removes intimidation</li>
</ul>

<h3>4. Lapsed &amp; Inactive Members (Re-engagement)</h3>
<p>They said yes once. We remind them why.</p>
<ul>
  <li>&ldquo;Welcome back&rdquo; email sequences and retargeting</li>
  <li>What's new since they last engaged</li>
  <li>Community-driven &ldquo;you're missed&rdquo; social proof</li>
</ul>

<h3>Insurance Messaging (Without Fear)</h3>
<p>Insurance is the number-one motivator, but fear-based messaging is off the table. We agree.</p>

<div class="comparison">
  <table style="border:none; margin:0;">
    <tr>
      <td style="border:none; padding:4pt 10pt; width:50%; vertical-align:top; color:#cc0000;">
        <span style="font-size:9pt; color:#cc0000;">NOT THIS:</span><br>
        &ldquo;Without insurance, one accident could cost you everything.&rdquo;
      </td>
      <td style="border:none; padding:4pt 10pt; width:50%; vertical-align:top; color:#0072bc;">
        <span style="font-size:9pt; color:#0072bc;">INSTEAD:</span><br>
        &ldquo;Responsible riders ride protected. AEF membership means $5M in liability coverage, so you can focus on what you love.&rdquo;
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- PAGE BREAK -->
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-special-character:line-break;">

